<title>UK: Amersham sees 250-300 combined job losses.</title>
<headline>Amersham sees 250-300 combined job losses.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>British health and technology group Amersham International Plc said on Tuesday it anticipated combined job losses of between 250 and 300 as a result of its planned merger with Norway's Nycomed ASA.</p>
<p>The two businesses, including Pharmacia Biotech which is merging with Amersham Life Sciences under separate plans announced last month, had total staff of around 11,500.  </p>
<p>In a telephone interview with Reuters, Amersham chief executive Bill Castell said the job cuts would come from reductions in administration and sales staff and site closures.</p>
<p>However Castell said that cost-savings, targeted at 40 million stg a year after three years, were not the &quot;key driver&quot; behind the proposed merger.</p>
<p>Other sources close to Amersham also told Reuters that there were &quot;indications from Norway that (Nycomed) shareholders are supportive of the merger.&quot;</p>
<p>--Jonathan Birt London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
